+## Usage accumulation
+
+- `afterModelResponse` receives the sum of `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` across every provider call in the turn, so a deployer using it for billing or audit records the full turn cost ([validated by: reports the summed usage of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- A provider call that reports no usage is excluded from the sum; a turn where no call reports usage passes `undefined` to the hook ([validated by: leaves out a round that reports no usage, and reports nothing when no round reports](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
+- The accumulator adds two `UsageMetadata` values field-by-field when both are defined ([validated by: sums two defined UsageMetadata values](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
+- When one operand is `undefined` the accumulator returns the other unchanged ([validated by: returns the defined value when the other is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L35)).
+- When both operands are `undefined` the accumulator returns `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when both are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
